Que 4. Draw an analogy between a SQLite database table and a real-world example from an app you use (e.g., an Instagram followers list or a Flipkart order history), describing what the table, rows, and columns would represent.

Ans :-) A SQLite database table is similar to the Order History section in the Flipkart app.

Table represents the complete Order History.
Rows represent each individual order placed by the customer.
Columns represent the details of each order, such as Order ID, Product Name, Price, Order Date, and Delivery Status.
Example
Order ID	Product Name	         Price    	Order Date   Delivery Status
     101 	Wireless Mouse   	     ₹599	      10-06-2026	   Delivered
     102	Bluetooth Speaker	     ₹1,499	    15-06-2026	   Shipped
     103	Mobile Cover	         ₹299	      20-06-2026	   Pending

Conclusion
Just like Flipkart stores every order in an organized table, SQLite stores application data in tables with rows and columns. This makes it easy to add, search, update, and manage information efficiently.
